{% comment %}
  Renders Purelane's price markup (current price, strikethrough compare-at,
  optional savings badge) in one of the three shapes used across sections.
  One implementation, three brand-accurate outputs — avoids hand-rolling the
  same money math three times.

  Accepts:
  - price: {Number|String} current price, in the shop's currency subunit-free
    decimal form (e.g. 499), OR pass `product` instead to read live values.
  - compare_at_price: {Number|String} original price before discount (optional)
  - product: {Object} a real product/variant — when passed, price and
    compare_at_price are read from it instead of the explicit params
    (use this on the Shop grid; use explicit price/compare_at on Combos and
    Bundle tiers, since those are flat metaobject-defined prices, not a
    single product's own price)
  - variant: {String} 'card' (.pr, %-off badge) | 'combo' (.prow, ₹-savings
    badge) | 'tier' (.price, no badge). Default 'card'.

  Usage:
  {% render 'purelane-price', product: card_product, variant: 'card' %}
  {% render 'purelane-price', price: combo.price.value, compare_at_price: combo.compare_at_price.value, variant: 'combo' %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign display_variant = variant | default: 'card'

  comment
    Every price here is in the currency's subunit (cents), which is what the
    `money` filter formats. A variant's own price already is, and so is a
    `money` metafield's .value — it looks like an object but coerces to
    subunits in arithmetic. A plain number section setting does NOT, so those
    call sites convert before rendering (see purelane-hero.liquid).
  endcomment
  if product
    assign target = product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: product
    assign resolved_price = target.price
    assign resolved_compare = target.compare_at_price
  else
    assign resolved_price = price
    assign resolved_compare = compare_at_price
  endif

  assign has_discount = false
  if resolved_compare > resolved_price
    assign has_discount = true
    assign savings = resolved_compare | minus: resolved_price
    assign savings_money = savings | money
    assign percent_off = savings | times: 100.0 | divided_by: resolved_compare | round
  endif
-%}
{%- case display_variant -%}
  {%- when 'combo' -%}
    <div class="purelane-prow">
      <strong>{{ resolved_price | money }}</strong>
      {%- if has_discount -%}
        <s>{{ resolved_compare | money }}</s>
        <em>{{ 'purelane.price.save_amount' | t: amount: savings_money }}</em>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- when 'tier' -%}
    <div class="purelane-tier-price">
      {{ resolved_price | money }}
      {%- if has_discount -%}
        <s>{{ resolved_compare | money }}</s>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="purelane-pr">
      <strong>{{ resolved_price | money }}</strong>
      {%- if has_discount -%}
        <s>{{ resolved_compare | money }}</s>
        <em>{{ percent_off }}% off</em>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
{%- endcase -%}
